{"type":"message","id":"ebbcd5ca","parentId":"5980d710","timestamp":"2026-05-18T11:05:24.662Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_B9iWI5MhMcR805smAcP0sSrR","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# SOUL.md — Pixel, the Image Creator\n\nYou are **Pixel** 🎨, an AI image generation specialist for a crypto news publication. You produce one editorial feature image per article using the Leonardo AI API via a hardened bash skill script.\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ CRITICAL RULES — READ BEFORE ANYTHING ELSE\n\n1. **You have a `bash` tool. You MUST USE IT.** Do not describe what you would do. Do not output fake file paths. Execute the actual commands below.\n2. **NEVER call the Leonardo AI API directly.** The skill script handles all API calls. Your only job is crafting the prompt and running the script.\n3. **NEVER invent or guess a file path.** The only valid success output is what `cat /tmp/image-result.txt` prints after the script exits 0.\n4. **Every step marked `[TOOL CALL REQUIRED]` must produce a real bash tool call.** No exceptions.\n\n---\n\n## Step 1 — Craft the Image Prompt\n\n<thinking>\nLook at the article title and topic. Match it to the closest Scene Template below. Pick the scene. Write the prompt following the formula exactly. Keep it under 300 characters. End with the required style suffix.\n</thinking>\n\n### The Formula (ALWAYS follow this)\n> [A real human subject doing/reacting to the story] + [specific crypto asset visually present in the scene] + editorial photography style\n\n### Hard Rules\n- **MUST feature at least one human being** — a trader, developer, executive, regulator, investor. Never zero people. NON-NEGOTIABLE.\n- **MUST include the relevant crypto asset visually** — Bitcoin logo on a screen, Ethereum chart on a monitor, DeFi interface visible on a browser.\n- Describe a real candid moment: what is the person doing, where are they, what is on their screen.\n- **End ALL prompts with exactly:** `editorial press photography, Reuters style, photorealistic, DSLR, 35mm lens, sharp focus, candid`\n- **NO TEXT in the prompt** — do not describe words, signs, labels, or numbers that should appear IN the image.\n- Do NOT describe circuit boards, abstract glowing shapes, or floating coins with no humans.\n- Keep the prompt under 300 characters.\n\n### Scene Templates (pick closest match)\n\n| Story Type | Scene to Describe |\n|---|---|\n| Price movement (BTC/ETH up or down) | Trader at multi-monitor desk, Bitcoin price chart on screen, trading floor background |\n| Regulation / government ban | Government official at podium or signing desk, cryptocurrency logos on projected screen |\n| Fork / protocol upgrade / developer news | Software developer at laptop in office, blockchain interface visible on screen |\n| ETF / institutional flows / investment | Financial analyst at Bloomberg terminal, Bitcoin or Ethereum ticker on display |\n| DeFi exploit / hack / security breach | Cybersecurity professional at dark workstation, Ethereum or DeFi dashboard visible on screen |\n| Exchange / trading platform news | Crypto exchange trader at desk, trading platform UI on monitor |\n| General crypto market | Investor looking at phone with crypto portfolio app, office or coffee shop background |\n\n### Universal Fallback\nIf unsure which template to use, ALWAYS default to:\n> `Focused male trader at multi-screen trading desk, Bitcoin price chart visible on monitor, dark professional office, editorial press photography, Reuters style, photorealistic, DSLR, 35mm lens, sharp focus, candid`\n\n---\n\n## Step 2 — Execute the Skill Script `[TOOL CALL REQUIRED]`\n\n<thinking>\nI have crafted my prompt. I will now execute the bash tool. I will NOT output the result — I will wait for the actual exit code from the script.\n</thinking>\n\nRun this **exact** command using your bash tool. Replace `<YOUR CRAFTED PROMPT>` with the prompt you crafted in Step 1:\n\n```bash\nbash ~/.openclaw/workspace-creator/skills/generate-image/generate.sh \"<YOUR CRAFTED PROMPT>\"\n```\n\n**WAIT for the script to finish. Do NOT skip this step. Do NOT guess the output.**\n\nThe script will handle everything: API submission, retries, polling (up to 60 seconds), image download, JPEG validation, and logo watermarking.\n\n---\n\n## Step 3 — Read the Result `[TOOL CALL REQUIRED]`\n\n<thinking>\nThe script has exited. I will now check the exit code and read the appropriate output file.\n</thinking>\n\n**If the script exited with code `0` (success):**\n```bash\ncat /tmp/image-result.txt\n```\nReturn the file path printed by that command. Nothing else.\n\n**If the script exited with code `1` (failure):**\n```bash\ncat /tmp/image-error.log\n```\nReturn exactly: `IMAGE_FAILED: <contents of error log>`\n\n---\n\n## Step 4 — Final Output\n\nReturn ONLY one of these two things:\n- The file path: `/tmp/crypto-feature.jpg`\n- Or: `IMAGE_FAILED: <reason from error log>`\n\n**No commentary. No explanation. No apology. Just the result.**\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779102324662}}
{"type":"message","id":"11f8d95e","parentId":"ebbcd5ca","timestamp":"2026-05-18T11:05:30.593Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I’ve got the article angle and the asset. I’m checking the image script path and then I’ll generate the feature image."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_Z9K3VisjbBD5sC6KZ4m6FaSZ","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"ls -l ~/.openclaw/workspace-creator/skills/generate-image/generate.sh && sed -n '1,220p' ~/.openclaw/workspace-creator/skills/generate-image/generate.sh","workdir":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-creator","yieldMs":1000,"timeout":10}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_QFkmsfd8HAUCFcKKxJXnc7Qu","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nprompt = 'Focused male trader at news terminal, reacting to Middle East crisis, Bitcoin price chart visible on monitor, tense newsroom trading desk, editorial press photography, Reuters style, photorealistic, DSLR, 35mm lens, sharp focus, candid'\nprint(len(prompt))\nPY","workdir":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-creator","yieldMs":1000,"timeout":10}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gpt-5.4-mini","usage":{"input":1194,"output":424,"cacheRead":6272,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":7890,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779102324662,"responseId":"chatcmpl-Dgq4msNkXPLeVqj4WmbsEpJhj3NDG"}}
{"type":"message","id":"278be9bd","parentId":"11f8d95e","timestamp":"2026-05-18T11:05:30.654Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_Z9K3VisjbBD5sC6KZ4m6FaSZ","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"-rwxr-xr-x 1 bhard bhard 7768 May  5 05:25 /home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-creator/skills/generate-image/generate.sh\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# =============================================================================\n# generate.sh — Leonardo AI Image Generation Skill for Pixel (Creator Agent)\n# =============================================================================\n# Usage:\n#   bash generate.sh \"<IMAGE PROMPT>\"\n#\n# Output:\n#   Exit 0 → /tmp/image-result.txt contains the file path\n#   Exit 1 → /tmp/image-error.log contains the human-readable error reason\n# =============================================================================\n\nset -euo pipefail\n\n# --- Config ------------------------------------------------------------------\nPROMPT=\"${1:-}\"\nAPI_KEY=\"dddd08ff-d8c3-4fec-98d9-9e8c060f4619\"\nMODEL_ID=\"b2614463-296c-462a-9586-aafdb8f00e36\"\nAPI_BASE=\"https://cloud.leonardo.ai/api/rest/v1\"\nOUTPUT_PATH=\"/tmp/crypto-feature.jpg\"\nRESULT_FILE=\"/tmp/image-result.txt\"\nERROR_FILE=\"/tmp/image-error.log\"\nLOGO_PATH=\"$HOME/.openclaw/assets/logo.png\"\nMAX_GENERATE_RETRIES=3\nPOLL_ATTEMPTS=6\nPOLL_INTERVAL=10  # seconds between polls (6 x 10s = 60s max)\n\n# --- Helpers -----------------------------------------------------------------\nlog_error() {\n  echo \"[ERROR] $*\" | tee -a \"$ERROR_FILE\"\n}\n\nlog_info() {\n  echo \"[INFO]  $*\"\n}\n\nfatal() {\n  log_error \"$*\"\n  exit 1\n}\n\n# --- Validate Input ----------------------------------------------------------\nrm -f \"$ERROR_FILE\" \"$RESULT_FILE\"\n\nif [ -z \"$PROMPT\" ]; then\n  fatal \"No prompt provided. Usage: bash generate.sh \\\"<prompt>\\\"\"\nfi\n\nif [ ${#PROMPT} -gt 1000 ]; then\n  fatal \"Prompt too long (${#PROMPT} chars). Max 1000 characters.\"\nfi\n\nlog_info \"Starting image generation for prompt: ${PROMPT:0:80}...\"\n\n# --- Phase 1: Submit Generation Request (with retry + backoff) ---------------\nGENERATION_ID=\"\"\nRETRY_DELAY=5\n\nfor attempt in $(seq 1 $MAX_GENERATE_RETRIES); do\n  log_info \"Generation attempt $attempt of $MAX_GENERATE_RETRIES...\"\n\n  HTTP_RESPONSE=$(curl --silent --write-out \"\\n__HTTP_STATUS__%{http_code}\" \\\n    --request POST \\\n    --url \"$API_BASE/generations\" \\\n    --header \"accept: application/json\" \\\n    --header \"authorization: Bearer $API_KEY\" \\\n    --header \"content-type: application/json\" \\\n    --data \"{\n      \\\"prompt\\\": $(echo \"$PROMPT\" | python3 -c 'import json,sys; print(json.dumps(sys.stdin.read().strip()))'),\n      \\\"modelId\\\": \\\"$MODEL_ID\\\",\n      \\\"num_images\\\": 1,\n      \\\"width\\\": 1024,\n      \\\"height\\\": 576\n    }\" \\\n    --max-time 30)\n\n  HTTP_BODY=$(echo \"$HTTP_RESPONSE\" | sed '$d')\n  HTTP_STATUS=$(echo \"$HTTP_RESPONSE\" | tail -1 | sed 's/__HTTP_STATUS__//')\n\n  log_info \"API response status: $HTTP_STATUS\"\n\n  # --- Error Classification ---\n  if [ \"$HTTP_STATUS\" = \"401\" ]; then\n    fatal \"Authentication failed (401). API key is invalid or expired. Not retrying.\"\n  fi\n\n  if [ \"$HTTP_STATUS\" = \"403\" ]; then\n    fatal \"Access forbidden (403). Account may be suspended or quota exceeded. Not retrying.\"\n  fi\n\n  if [ \"$HTTP_STATUS\" = \"422\" ]; then\n    fatal \"Invalid request (422). The prompt may contain disallowed content. Body: $HTTP_BODY. Not retrying.\"\n  fi\n\n  if [ \"$HTTP_STATUS\" = \"200\" ] || [ \"$HTTP_STATUS\" = \"201\" ]; then\n    # Success — extract generationId\n    GENERATION_ID=$(echo \"$HTTP_BODY\" | python3 -c \"\nimport json, sys\ndata = json.load(sys.stdin)\ngen = data.get('sdGenerationJob', {})\ngid = gen.get('generationId', '')\nprint(gid)\n\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"\")\n\n    if [ -n \"$GENERATION_ID\" ]; then\n      log_info \"Generation submitted. ID: $GENERATION_ID\"\n      break\n    else\n      log_error \"Got HTTP 200 but no generationId in response. Body: ${HTTP_BODY:0:200}\"\n    fi\n  fi\n\n  # Transient failure (5xx, 429, network issue) — retry with backoff\n  log_error \"Transient error (status=$HTTP_STATUS). Waiting ${RETRY_DELAY}s before retry...\"\n  sleep $RETRY_DELAY\n  RETRY_DELAY=$((RETRY_DELAY * 2))  # Exponential backoff: 5s, 10s, 20s\ndone\n\nif [ -z \"$GENERATION_ID\" ]; then\n  fatal \"Failed to submit generation after $MAX_GENERATE_RETRIES attempts. Giving up.\"\nfi\n\n# --- Phase 2: Poll for Completion (up to 60 seconds) -------------------------\nlog_info \"Polling for generation completion (max ${POLL_ATTEMPTS} polls x ${POLL_INTERVAL}s = $((POLL_ATTEMPTS * POLL_INTERVAL))s)...\"\n\nIMAGE_URL=\"\"\nfor poll in $(seq 1 $POLL_ATTEMPTS); do\n  sleep $POLL_INTERVAL\n\n  log_info \"Poll $poll of $POLL_ATTEMPTS...\"\n\n  POLL_RESPONSE=$(curl --silent --write-out \"\\n__HTTP_STATUS__%{http_code}\" \\\n    --request GET \\\n    --url \"$API_BASE/generations/$GENERATION_ID\" \\\n    --header \"authorization: Bearer $API_KEY\" \\\n    --max-time 15)\n\n  POLL_BODY=$(echo \"$POLL_RESPONSE\" | sed '$d')\n  POLL_STATUS=$(echo \"$POLL_RESPONSE\" | tail -1 | sed 's/__HTTP_STATUS__//')\n\n  if [ \"$POLL_STATUS\" != \"200\" ]; then\n    log_error \"Poll $poll returned HTTP $POLL_STATUS. Will retry...\"\n    continue\n  fi\n\n  IMAGE_URL=$(echo \"$POLL_BODY\" | python3 -c \"\nimport json, sys\ndata = json.load(sys.stdin)\ngen = data.get('generations_by_pk', {})\nimages = gen.get('generated_images', [])\nif images:\n    print(images[0].get('url', ''))\n\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"\")\n\n  if [ -n \"$IMAGE_URL\" ]; then\n    log_info \"Image ready! URL: ${IMAGE_URL:0:80}...\"\n    break\n  else\n    log_info \"Image not ready yet. Generation status: $(echo \"$POLL_BODY\" | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d.get('generations_by_pk',{}).get('status','unknown'))\" 2>/dev/null || echo 'unknown')\"\n  fi\ndone\n\nif [ -z \"$IMAGE_URL\" ]; then\n  fatal \"Image generation timed out after $((POLL_ATTEMPTS * POLL_INTERVAL)) seconds. GenerationId: $GENERATION_ID\"\nfi\n\n# --- Phase 3: Download & Validate --------------------------------------------\nlog_info \"Downloading image to $OUTPUT_PATH...\"\n\nHTTP_DL_STATUS=$(curl --silent --location --write-out \"%{http_code}\" \\\n  --output \"$OUTPUT_PATH\" \\\n  --max-time 60 \\\n  \"$IMAGE_URL\")\n\nif [ \"$HTTP_DL_STATUS\" != \"200\" ]; then\n  fatal \"Download failed with HTTP $HTTP_DL_STATUS. URL: $IMAGE_URL\"\nfi\n\nif [ ! -f \"$OUTPUT_PATH\" ]; then\n  fatal \"Downloaded file does not exist at $OUTPUT_PATH\"\nfi\n\nFILE_SIZE=$(stat -c%s \"$OUTPUT_PATH\" 2>/dev/null || stat -f%z \"$OUTPUT_PATH\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"0\")\nif [ \"$FILE_SIZE\" -lt 51200 ]; then  # Less than 50KB\n  fatal \"Downloaded file is too small (${FILE_SIZE} bytes). Likely a corrupted or error response image.\"\nfi\n\n# Validate it's actually a JPEG\nFILE_TYPE=$(file -b \"$OUTPUT_PATH\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"unknown\")\nif ! echo \"$FILE_TYPE\" | grep -qi \"JPEG\\|jpg\"; then\n  log_error \"WARNING: File type check returned: $FILE_TYPE — may not be a valid JPEG, but proceeding.\"\nfi\n\nlog_info \"Image downloaded successfully. Size: ${FILE_SIZE} bytes. Type: ${FILE_TYPE:0:30}\"\n\n# --- Phase 4: Logo Stamping (non-fatal) --------------------------------------\nif command -v convert &>/dev/null; then\n  if [ -f \"$LOGO_PATH\" ]; then\n    log_info \"Stamping logo onto image...\"\n    TEMP_LOGO=\"/tmp/temp_logo_$$.png\"\n\n    if convert \"$LOGO_PATH\" -resize 150x \"$TEMP_LOGO\" 2>/dev/null && \\\n       composite -gravity SouthEast -geometry +20+20 \"$TEMP_LOGO\" \"$OUTPUT_PATH\" \"$OUTPUT_PATH\" 2>/dev/null; then\n      log_info \"Logo stamped successfully.\"\n    else\n      log_error \"WARNING: Logo stamping failed — image saved without watermark. Continuing.\"\n    fi\n\n    rm -f \"$TEMP_LOGO\"\n  else\n    log_error \"WARNING: Logo not found at $LOGO_PATH — skipping watermark. Continuing.\"\n  fi\nelse\n  log_error \"WARNING: ImageMagick (convert) not installed — skipping watermark. Continuing.\"\nfi\n\n# --- Phase 5: Final Verification & Output ------------------------------------\nFINAL_SIZE=$(stat -c%s \"$OUTPUT_PATH\" 2>/dev/null || stat -f%z \"$OUTPUT_PATH\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"0\")\nlog_info \"Final image at $OUTPUT_PATH — size: ${FINAL_SIZE} bytes\""}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":32,"aggregated":"-rwxr-xr-x 1 bhard bhard 7768 May  5 05:25 /home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-creator/skills/generate-image/generate.sh\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# =============================================================================\n# generate.sh — Leonardo AI Image Generation Skill for Pixel (Creator Agent)\n# =============================================================================\n# Usage:\n#   bash generate.sh \"<IMAGE PROMPT>\"\n#\n# Output:\n#   Exit 0 → /tmp/image-result.txt contains the file path\n#   Exit 1 → /tmp/image-error.log contains the human-readable error reason\n# =============================================================================\n\nset -euo pipefail\n\n# --- Config ------------------------------------------------------------------\nPROMPT=\"${1:-}\"\nAPI_KEY=\"dddd08ff-d8c3-4fec-98d9-9e8c060f4619\"\nMODEL_ID=\"b2614463-296c-462a-9586-aafdb8f00e36\"\nAPI_BASE=\"https://cloud.leonardo.ai/api/rest/v1\"\nOUTPUT_PATH=\"/tmp/crypto-feature.jpg\"\nRESULT_FILE=\"/tmp/image-result.txt\"\nERROR_FILE=\"/tmp/image-error.log\"\nLOGO_PATH=\"$HOME/.openclaw/assets/logo.png\"\nMAX_GENERATE_RETRIES=3\nPOLL_ATTEMPTS=6\nPOLL_INTERVAL=10  # seconds between polls (6 x 10s = 60s max)\n\n# --- Helpers -----------------------------------------------------------------\nlog_error() {\n  echo \"[ERROR] $*\" | tee -a \"$ERROR_FILE\"\n}\n\nlog_info() {\n  echo \"[INFO]  $*\"\n}\n\nfatal() {\n  log_error \"$*\"\n  exit 1\n}\n\n# --- Validate Input ----------------------------------------------------------\nrm -f \"$ERROR_FILE\" \"$RESULT_FILE\"\n\nif [ -z \"$PROMPT\" ]; then\n  fatal \"No prompt provided. Usage: bash generate.sh \\\"<prompt>\\\"\"\nfi\n\nif [ ${#PROMPT} -gt 1000 ]; then\n  fatal \"Prompt too long (${#PROMPT} chars). Max 1000 characters.\"\nfi\n\nlog_info \"Starting image generation for prompt: ${PROMPT:0:80}...\"\n\n# --- Phase 1: Submit Generation Request (with retry + backoff) ---------------\nGENERATION_ID=\"\"\nRETRY_DELAY=5\n\nfor attempt in $(seq 1 $MAX_GENERATE_RETRIES); do\n  log_info \"Generation attempt $attempt of $MAX_GENERATE_RETRIES...\"\n\n  HTTP_RESPONSE=$(curl --silent --write-out \"\\n__HTTP_STATUS__%{http_code}\" \\\n    --request POST \\\n    --url \"$API_BASE/generations\" \\\n    --header \"accept: application/json\" \\\n    --header \"authorization: Bearer $API_KEY\" \\\n    --header \"content-type: application/json\" \\\n    --data \"{\n      \\\"prompt\\\": $(echo \"$PROMPT\" | python3 -c 'import json,sys; print(json.dumps(sys.stdin.read().strip()))'),\n      \\\"modelId\\\": \\\"$MODEL_ID\\\",\n      \\\"num_images\\\": 1,\n      \\\"width\\\": 1024,\n      \\\"height\\\": 576\n    }\" \\\n    --max-time 30)\n\n  HTTP_BODY=$(echo \"$HTTP_RESPONSE\" | sed '$d')\n  HTTP_STATUS=$(echo \"$HTTP_RESPONSE\" | tail -1 | sed 's/__HTTP_STATUS__//')\n\n  log_info \"API response status: $HTTP_STATUS\"\n\n  # --- Error Classification ---\n  if [ \"$HTTP_STATUS\" = \"401\" ]; then\n    fatal \"Authentication failed (401). API key is invalid or expired. Not retrying.\"\n  fi\n\n  if [ \"$HTTP_STATUS\" = \"403\" ]; then\n    fatal \"Access forbidden (403). Account may be suspended or quota exceeded. Not retrying.\"\n  fi\n\n  if [ \"$HTTP_STATUS\" = \"422\" ]; then\n    fatal \"Invalid request (422). The prompt may contain disallowed content. Body: $HTTP_BODY. Not retrying.\"\n  fi\n\n  if [ \"$HTTP_STATUS\" = \"200\" ] || [ \"$HTTP_STATUS\" = \"201\" ]; then\n    # Success — extract generationId\n    GENERATION_ID=$(echo \"$HTTP_BODY\" | python3 -c \"\nimport json, sys\ndata = json.load(sys.stdin)\ngen = data.get('sdGenerationJob', {})\ngid = gen.get('generationId', '')\nprint(gid)\n\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"\")\n\n    if [ -n \"$GENERATION_ID\" ]; then\n      log_info \"Generation submitted. ID: $GENERATION_ID\"\n      break\n    else\n      log_error \"Got HTTP 200 but no generationId in response. Body: ${HTTP_BODY:0:200}\"\n    fi\n  fi\n\n  # Transient failure (5xx, 429, network issue) — retry with backoff\n  log_error \"Transient error (status=$HTTP_STATUS). Waiting ${RETRY_DELAY}s before retry...\"\n  sleep $RETRY_DELAY\n  RETRY_DELAY=$((RETRY_DELAY * 2))  # Exponential backoff: 5s, 10s, 20s\ndone\n\nif [ -z \"$GENERATION_ID\" ]; then\n  fatal \"Failed to submit generation after $MAX_GENERATE_RETRIES attempts. Giving up.\"\nfi\n\n# --- Phase 2: Poll for Completion (up to 60 seconds) -------------------------\nlog_info \"Polling for generation completion (max ${POLL_ATTEMPTS} polls x ${POLL_INTERVAL}s = $((POLL_ATTEMPTS * POLL_INTERVAL))s)...\"\n\nIMAGE_URL=\"\"\nfor poll in $(seq 1 $POLL_ATTEMPTS); do\n  sleep $POLL_INTERVAL\n\n  log_info \"Poll $poll of $POLL_ATTEMPTS...\"\n\n  POLL_RESPONSE=$(curl --silent --write-out \"\\n__HTTP_STATUS__%{http_code}\" \\\n    --request GET \\\n    --url \"$API_BASE/generations/$GENERATION_ID\" \\\n    --header \"authorization: Bearer $API_KEY\" \\\n    --max-time 15)\n\n  POLL_BODY=$(echo \"$POLL_RESPONSE\" | sed '$d')\n  POLL_STATUS=$(echo \"$POLL_RESPONSE\" | tail -1 | sed 's/__HTTP_STATUS__//')\n\n  if [ \"$POLL_STATUS\" != \"200\" ]; then\n    log_error \"Poll $poll returned HTTP $POLL_STATUS. Will retry...\"\n    continue\n  fi\n\n  IMAGE_URL=$(echo \"$POLL_BODY\" | python3 -c \"\nimport json, sys\ndata = json.load(sys.stdin)\ngen = data.get('generations_by_pk', {})\nimages = gen.get('generated_images', [])\nif images:\n    print(images[0].get('url', ''))\n\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"\")\n\n  if [ -n \"$IMAGE_URL\" ]; then\n    log_info \"Image ready! URL: ${IMAGE_URL:0:80}...\"\n    break\n  else\n    log_info \"Image not ready yet. Generation status: $(echo \"$POLL_BODY\" | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d.get('generations_by_pk',{}).get('status','unknown'))\" 2>/dev/null || echo 'unknown')\"\n  fi\ndone\n\nif [ -z \"$IMAGE_URL\" ]; then\n  fatal \"Image generation timed out after $((POLL_ATTEMPTS * POLL_INTERVAL)) seconds. GenerationId: $GENERATION_ID\"\nfi\n\n# --- Phase 3: Download & Validate --------------------------------------------\nlog_info \"Downloading image to $OUTPUT_PATH...\"\n\nHTTP_DL_STATUS=$(curl --silent --location --write-out \"%{http_code}\" \\\n  --output \"$OUTPUT_PATH\" \\\n  --max-time 60 \\\n  \"$IMAGE_URL\")\n\nif [ \"$HTTP_DL_STATUS\" != \"200\" ]; then\n  fatal \"Download failed with HTTP $HTTP_DL_STATUS. URL: $IMAGE_URL\"\nfi\n\nif [ ! -f \"$OUTPUT_PATH\" ]; then\n  fatal \"Downloaded file does not exist at $OUTPUT_PATH\"\nfi\n\nFILE_SIZE=$(stat -c%s \"$OUTPUT_PATH\" 2>/dev/null || stat -f%z \"$OUTPUT_PATH\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"0\")\nif [ \"$FILE_SIZE\" -lt 51200 ]; then  # Less than 50KB\n  fatal \"Downloaded file is too small (${FILE_SIZE} bytes). Likely a corrupted or error response image.\"\nfi\n\n# Validate it's actually a JPEG\nFILE_TYPE=$(file -b \"$OUTPUT_PATH\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"unknown\")\nif ! echo \"$FILE_TYPE\" | grep -qi \"JPEG\\|jpg\"; then\n  log_error \"WARNING: File type check returned: $FILE_TYPE — may not be a valid JPEG, but proceeding.\"\nfi\n\nlog_info \"Image downloaded successfully. Size: ${FILE_SIZE} bytes. Type: ${FILE_TYPE:0:30}\"\n\n# --- Phase 4: Logo Stamping (non-fatal) --------------------------------------\nif command -v convert &>/dev/null; then\n  if [ -f \"$LOGO_PATH\" ]; then\n    log_info \"Stamping logo onto image...\"\n    TEMP_LOGO=\"/tmp/temp_logo_$$.png\"\n\n    if convert \"$LOGO_PATH\" -resize 150x \"$TEMP_LOGO\" 2>/dev/null && \\\n       composite -gravity SouthEast -geometry +20+20 \"$TEMP_LOGO\" \"$OUTPUT_PATH\" \"$OUTPUT_PATH\" 2>/dev/null; then\n      log_info \"Logo stamped successfully.\"\n    else\n      log_error \"WARNING: Logo stamping failed — image saved without watermark. Continuing.\"\n    fi\n\n    rm -f \"$TEMP_LOGO\"\n  else\n    log_error \"WARNING: Logo not found at $LOGO_PATH — skipping watermark. Continuing.\"\n  fi\nelse\n  log_error \"WARNING: ImageMagick (convert) not installed — skipping watermark. Continuing.\"\nfi\n\n# --- Phase 5: Final Verification & Output ------------------------------------\nFINAL_SIZE=$(stat -c%s \"$OUTPUT_PATH\" 2>/dev/null || stat -f%z \"$OUTPUT_PATH\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"0\")\nlog_info \"Final image at $OUTPUT_PATH — size: ${FINAL_SIZE} bytes\"","cwd":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-creator"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779102330654}}
